    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `mvn test` build passed (BUILD SUCCESS) with both tests green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date behaviour: when no registration date is supplied on `POST /api/owners`, it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes (kept as small, cohesive units to minimize structural impact):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added one optional `registrationDate` field (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf: [OwnerFields, \u2026]`, this single edit gives both the input DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the output DTO (`OwnerDto`) the field automatically. A `date`-format field serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` column plus a plain getter/setter (CC 1 each). No logic added to the entity's existing methods.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a single MapStruct `@Mapping` with `defaultExpression = \"java(java.time.LocalDate.now())\"` on the create path (`toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`). This puts the \"default to today\" rule in the small mapper class rather than in the larger entity, and MapStruct maps the field back out to the DTO automatically by name. No new method or branch was written by hand.\n\n4. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 Added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table across all four supported DBs (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) for consistency, and appended a `NULL` value to the positional seed inserts in `hsqldb` and `mysql` data files (the h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists, so they needed no change).\n\n**Result:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS; both acceptance tests (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass.",
